      "interpretation": "Evaluate conditional casing against original text. Canonical combining class zero/230 bounds After_I, After_Soft_Dotted, Before_Dot and More_Above; case-ignorable precedence still controls Final_Sigma."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/SpecialCasing.txt",
      "interpretation": "Apply Turkic dot/dotless-I and Lithuanian soft-dot/above-accent mappings, including zero- and three-unit results. Other content languages remain explicit until their tailoring is qualified."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG2/text.html#TermAddressableCharacter",
      "interpretation": "Positioning indices precede case conversion. Zero-emission absolute positions/rotations have no glyph target. Relative displacement transfers to the next surviving character, following the existing SVG treatment of nonglyph source components; this zero-emission extension is an explicit interpretation, not a pinned-browser indexing agreement."
    }
  ],
  "implementation": {
    "casing": "The existing context retains original word/case/combining state. Projection and streaming use the same lookahead predicates. Streaming holds one scalar/font binding, rather than retaining the text or an accent run. Empty needs do not enumerate a font selection or acquire a source.",
    "projection": "Drop empty spacing/paint/font/placement spans. Retain original scalar addresses for positions; merge relative offsets and reject overflow, discard deleted absolute/rotation operands and avoid reading an emitted-end rune. Keep actual element identities across node deletion. Re-find surviving directly painted recording text while skipping descendant scopes.",
    "paths": "Each range borrows its measured path and offset from the pending owner. Projection can remove an empty path range without reindexing a parallel measured-path array. Remove an endpoint transfer when its source path emitted no glyph. Original ranges retain every measured path until all views finish, then dispose on every exit.",
    "preserved": "No glyph-layout/GSUB/GPOS implementation change, font-name patch, tolerance change or reference rewrite. Existing unconditional mapping/word corpora are byte-identical; cased/ignorable bits remain identical at every old/new property boundary."
  },
